122:- **L2 — One-glyph population scaling.** Class: technique. Consumer: DLC assembler — diagram container. Change: adopt a single icon whose array size carries quantity (1 → 40 → full panel) so statistics scenes need no new artwork per scale. Build cost: cheap — one SVG icon + array layout rules.
123:- **L3 — Dashed = unrealized notation.** Class: texture. Consumer: Academy/Earth One production — diagram + ending containers. Change: reserve dashed outlines for future/hoped/unrealized states and solid for the actual, everywhere; the verdict frame (dashed larger self behind solid present self) becomes a reusable ending composition. Build cost: cheap — a line-style rule, no new assets.
126:- **L6 — Chart-as-argument, both directions.** Class: technique. Consumer: DLC assembler — diagram container. Change: when an episode must reverse its claim, run the reversal on the SAME chart that proved the claim (series added, verdict card updated), never on a new visual. Build cost: moderate — the chart must be built as a stateful component from the start.
